"""grounded_coord_ring policy (rendered from policy_template.py by gen_tables.py).

Seat roles
----------
* agent_1 (inner room) is the only seat that can cook and deliver.  It is
  fully self-sufficient: it reads the target recipe from any active button
  display it can see (whoever pressed it) and, if none is visible after a
  delivery, presses the button itself.  It never guesses the recipe from the
  partner's position, so a wrong delivery (-20) is never risked.
* agent_0 (outer ring) can see the always-on recipe indicators for free but
  cannot touch pot, plates or delivery.  It stands next to the button on the
  side matching the recipe (top row for ingredient 0, bottom row for
  ingredient 1) and presses the button for the partner only when the partner
  appears to need it (episode start, after a detected recipe change, or a
  long timeout while the partner is demonstrably working).  As soon as the
  partner is observed pressing the button itself, agent_0 stops pressing for
  the rest of the episode so no button cost is duplicated.

All tables are literal constants; runtime code is pure JAX with fixed-shape
control flow.
"""

